[{"source" ":org/Math-Academy" "forms" [[:db/retract 17592186155667 :answer-field/choices 17592186155668] [:db/retract 17592186155667 :answer-field/choices 17592186155669] [:db/retract 17592186155667 :answer-field/choices 17592186155670] [:db/retract 17592186155667 :answer-field/choices 17592186155671] [:db/retract 17592186155667 :answer-field/choices 17592186155672] {:db/id 17592186157791 :question/problem "Find ${f}^{″}(x,y)$ for the function $f(x,y)$ given that\n${f}^{′}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}-y & -x\\end{aligned}]$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R,$ given by\n\n$$\nf:{{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}⟶f({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nthe second derivative of $f$ is given by the $n\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}^{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that since ${f}^{′}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}-y & -x\\end{aligned}],$ we must have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=3{x}^{2}-y,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=-x.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the second partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(3{x}^{2}-y)=6x\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(-x)=-1 \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(3{x}^{2}-y)=-1\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(-x)=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}6x & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186155667 :answer-field/correct "answer-7cfd7658-f969-5d24-b54b-e78400ec350a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-42ad8ac2-0cae-5d02-b554-16bcbaa98c5d" "answer-9734b10a-54a0-50b1-8bf9-29f1e1b884d0" "answer-77498169-1361-5d9a-8c47-6032457435c9" "answer-7cfd7658-f969-5d24-b54b-e78400ec350a" "answer-1845ba91-aa39-523c-b7fb-24b0540f22a4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-42ad8ac2-0cae-5d02-b554-16bcbaa98c5d" :answer/id #uuid "42ad8ac2-0cae-5d02-b554-16bcbaa98c5d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & -x\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9734b10a-54a0-50b1-8bf9-29f1e1b884d0" :answer/id #uuid "9734b10a-54a0-50b1-8bf9-29f1e1b884d0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}-y & -1 \\\\ -1 & -x\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-77498169-1361-5d9a-8c47-6032457435c9" :answer/id #uuid "77498169-1361-5d9a-8c47-6032457435c9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}-y & -x \\\\ -x & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7cfd7658-f969-5d24-b54b-e78400ec350a" :answer/id #uuid "7cfd7658-f969-5d24-b54b-e78400ec350a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}6x & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1845ba91-aa39-523c-b7fb-24b0540f22a4" :answer/id #uuid "1845ba91-aa39-523c-b7fb-24b0540f22a4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}6x & -x \\\\ -x & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186157425 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-b2d69fc5-a88d-5940-a2a9-d7cc001b13e7" "question-46310383-5e9b-5711-9143-446211dee40a" "question-0614088a-4b37-5f45-a256-f7dd1a417f0a"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-b2d69fc5-a88d-5940-a2a9-d7cc001b13e7" :question/id #uuid "b2d69fc5-a88d-5940-a2a9-d7cc001b13e7" :question/math-academy-id "q-81033" :question/problem "Find ${f}^{″}(1,\\pi )$ for the function $f(x,y)={x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y.$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R,$ given by\n\n$$\nf:{{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}⟶f({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nthe second derivative of $f$ is given by the $n\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}^{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the first derivative of $f(x,y),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x,y) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & \\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y) & \\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y & {x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the second partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y)=2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)=2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y)=-{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x,y) & =[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡y & 2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y \\\\ 2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y & -{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate this matrix at $(1,\\pi ).$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(1,\\pi )=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-dc17abaf-f11c-5b72-9671-ca1fd6cb7d81"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-dc17abaf-f11c-5b72-9671-ca1fd6cb7d81" :answer-field/id #uuid "dc17abaf-f11c-5b72-9671-ca1fd6cb7d81" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-5c6f1e5c-0d83-5707-9be7-6186e6c7f868" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ba9c170b-091c-52e8-887d-30f59a09cad0" "answer-62703d69-369b-5ace-a8d1-0c23e81a72c7" "answer-5c6f1e5c-0d83-5707-9be7-6186e6c7f868" "answer-8a6bad3b-8668-59c6-b072-43c794a5f205" "answer-359a8021-5740-5c7d-85ad-b70c09368f55"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ba9c170b-091c-52e8-887d-30f59a09cad0" :answer/id #uuid "ba9c170b-091c-52e8-887d-30f59a09cad0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-62703d69-369b-5ace-a8d1-0c23e81a72c7" :answer/id #uuid "62703d69-369b-5ace-a8d1-0c23e81a72c7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5c6f1e5c-0d83-5707-9be7-6186e6c7f868" :answer/id #uuid "5c6f1e5c-0d83-5707-9be7-6186e6c7f868" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8a6bad3b-8668-59c6-b072-43c794a5f205" :answer/id #uuid "8a6bad3b-8668-59c6-b072-43c794a5f205" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-359a8021-5740-5c7d-85ad-b70c09368f55" :answer/id #uuid "359a8021-5740-5c7d-85ad-b70c09368f55" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-46310383-5e9b-5711-9143-446211dee40a" :question/id #uuid "46310383-5e9b-5711-9143-446211dee40a" :question/math-academy-id "q-80945" :question/problem "Find ${f}^{″}(0,-\\frac{\\pi }{2})$ for the function $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x-y).$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R,$ given by\n\n$$\nf:{{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}⟶f({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nthe second derivative of $f$ is given by the $n\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}^{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the first derivative of $f(x,y),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x,y) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & \\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x-y)) & \\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x-y))\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x-y) & -\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x-y)\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the second partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x-y))=-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x-y)\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x-y))=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x-y) \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x-y))=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x-y)\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x-y))=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x-y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x,y) & =[\\begin{aligned}-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x-y) & 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x-y) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x-y) & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x-y)\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate this matrix at $(0,-\\frac{\\pi }{2}).$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(0,-\\frac{\\pi }{2})=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a8dc6b69-1ae0-561f-a21b-1f490d47e054"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a8dc6b69-1ae0-561f-a21b-1f490d47e054" :answer-field/id #uuid "a8dc6b69-1ae0-561f-a21b-1f490d47e054" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-df6ec264-721c-5c32-b562-4dd7d6f6e9fb" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9df6896f-980a-5433-b50d-177ed45dbdf5" "answer-81e448c4-be6f-5b7c-9911-58f7b720cb69" "answer-7e106318-5cd1-562e-bb83-a7e1e65c6c69" "answer-df6ec264-721c-5c32-b562-4dd7d6f6e9fb" "answer-3317f54b-1416-55a3-8ca3-d53a13390c95"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9df6896f-980a-5433-b50d-177ed45dbdf5" :answer/id #uuid "9df6896f-980a-5433-b50d-177ed45dbdf5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-81e448c4-be6f-5b7c-9911-58f7b720cb69" :answer/id #uuid "81e448c4-be6f-5b7c-9911-58f7b720cb69" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7e106318-5cd1-562e-bb83-a7e1e65c6c69" :answer/id #uuid "7e106318-5cd1-562e-bb83-a7e1e65c6c69" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-df6ec264-721c-5c32-b562-4dd7d6f6e9fb" :answer/id #uuid "df6ec264-721c-5c32-b562-4dd7d6f6e9fb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3317f54b-1416-55a3-8ca3-d53a13390c95" :answer/id #uuid "3317f54b-1416-55a3-8ca3-d53a13390c95" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-0614088a-4b37-5f45-a256-f7dd1a417f0a" :question/id #uuid "0614088a-4b37-5f45-a256-f7dd1a417f0a" :question/math-academy-id "q-80943" :question/problem "Find ${f}^{″}(x,y)$ for the function $f(x,y)={e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y.$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R,$ given by\n\n$$\nf:{{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}⟶f({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nthe second derivative of $f$ is given by the $n\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}^{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the first derivative of $f(x,y),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x,y) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & \\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y) & \\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y & {e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the second partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)={e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y)={e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)={e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y)=-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x,y) & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y & {e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y \\\\ {e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y & -{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-7c34ea07-7e19-56a7-ba03-b874c7a7954b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-7c34ea07-7e19-56a7-ba03-b874c7a7954b" :answer-field/id #uuid "7c34ea07-7e19-56a7-ba03-b874c7a7954b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f08cd101-4751-528e-9c91-8bd8e073764f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-88aa9963-0fec-593b-849b-6f365aef81b0" "answer-af47d397-3313-5f02-895b-4079622ccc89" "answer-695ca77d-0c24-5a11-989b-13dbb21f08ac" "answer-9b60e2a2-ee1f-5fb2-9669-c7f3d20a997a" "answer-f08cd101-4751-528e-9c91-8bd8e073764f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-88aa9963-0fec-593b-849b-6f365aef81b0" :answer/id #uuid "88aa9963-0fec-593b-849b-6f365aef81b0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y & {e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y \\\\ {e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y & {e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-af47d397-3313-5f02-895b-4079622ccc89" :answer/id #uuid "af47d397-3313-5f02-895b-4079622ccc89" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y & -{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y \\\\ {e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y & {e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-695ca77d-0c24-5a11-989b-13dbb21f08ac" :answer/id #uuid "695ca77d-0c24-5a11-989b-13dbb21f08ac" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y & {e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y \\\\ -{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y & {e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9b60e2a2-ee1f-5fb2-9669-c7f3d20a997a" :answer/id #uuid "9b60e2a2-ee1f-5fb2-9669-c7f3d20a997a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y & \\operatorname{cos}⁡y \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡y & -{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f08cd101-4751-528e-9c91-8bd8e073764f" :answer/id #uuid "f08cd101-4751-528e-9c91-8bd8e073764f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y & {e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y \\\\ {e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y & -{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186157424 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-223797a4-3fdc-5efb-a9f2-b733398cd415"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-223797a4-3fdc-5efb-a9f2-b733398cd415" :question/id #uuid "223797a4-3fdc-5efb-a9f2-b733398cd415" :question/math-academy-id "q-80946" :question/problem "Given that \n${f}^{′}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}-{e}^{y}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & {e}^{y}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\end{aligned}],$ \nevaluate the Hessian determinant of $f(x,y)$ at the point $(0,0).$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R,$ given by\n\n$$\nf:{{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}⟶f({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nthe second derivative of $f$ is given by the $n\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}^{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe Hessian determinant $H(x,y)$ is the determinant of the second derivative:\n\n$$\nH(x)=det({f}^{″}(x))\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that since ${f}^{′}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}-{e}^{y}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & {e}^{y}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\end{aligned}],$ we must have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=-{e}^{y}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}={e}^{y}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the second partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(-{e}^{y}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)=-{e}^{y}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{y}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)=-{e}^{y}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(-{e}^{y}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)=-{e}^{y}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{y}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)={e}^{y}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x,y) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-{e}^{y}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x & -{e}^{y}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ -{e}^{y}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & {e}^{y}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating the second derivative at $(0,0),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(0,0)=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\nH(0,0)=(-1)\\cdot 1-{0}^{2}=-1.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e7c15a59-5adc-5127-8074-bf8ca6a5dc2b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e7c15a59-5adc-5127-8074-bf8ca6a5dc2b" :answer-field/id #uuid "e7c15a59-5adc-5127-8074-bf8ca6a5dc2b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-81decfb0-353d-554c-a766-c2d475210694" :answer-field/choices ["answer-81decfb0-353d-554c-a766-c2d475210694" "answer-c08ac167-4934-5d02-a974-ed7fd8f64367" "answer-06acb265-9aa4-5e5c-afdc-84b8445440f4" "answer-17e65082-0896-55d8-99e6-6536ee35ed4d" "answer-9f7d0305-07ee-5c49-a171-c47f7420e291"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-81decfb0-353d-554c-a766-c2d475210694" :answer/id #uuid "81decfb0-353d-554c-a766-c2d475210694" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c08ac167-4934-5d02-a974-ed7fd8f64367" :answer/id #uuid "c08ac167-4934-5d02-a974-ed7fd8f64367" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-06acb265-9aa4-5e5c-afdc-84b8445440f4" :answer/id #uuid "06acb265-9aa4-5e5c-afdc-84b8445440f4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-17e65082-0896-55d8-99e6-6536ee35ed4d" :answer/id #uuid "17e65082-0896-55d8-99e6-6536ee35ed4d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9f7d0305-07ee-5c49-a171-c47f7420e291" :answer/id #uuid "9f7d0305-07ee-5c49-a171-c47f7420e291" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]}] "assertions" [[17592186157791 :question/problem "Find ${f}^{″}(x,y)$ for the function $f(x,y)$ given that\n${f}^{′}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}-y & -x\\end{aligned}]$"] [17592186157791 :question/worked-solution "For a function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R,$ given by\n\n$$\nf:{{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}⟶f({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nthe second derivative of $f$ is given by the $n\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}^{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that since ${f}^{′}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}-y & -x\\end{aligned}],$ we must have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=3{x}^{2}-y,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=-x.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the second partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(3{x}^{2}-y)=6x\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(-x)=-1 \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(3{x}^{2}-y)=-1\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(-x)=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}6x & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186157791 :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-42ad8ac2-0cae-5d02-b554-16bcbaa98c5d" :answer/id #uuid "42ad8ac2-0cae-5d02-b554-16bcbaa98c5d"] ["answer-42ad8ac2-0cae-5d02-b554-16bcbaa98c5d" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-42ad8ac2-0cae-5d02-b554-16bcbaa98c5d" :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & -x\\end{aligned}]"] ["answer-9734b10a-54a0-50b1-8bf9-29f1e1b884d0" :answer/id #uuid "9734b10a-54a0-50b1-8bf9-29f1e1b884d0"] ["answer-9734b10a-54a0-50b1-8bf9-29f1e1b884d0" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-9734b10a-54a0-50b1-8bf9-29f1e1b884d0" :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}-y & -1 \\\\ -1 & -x\\end{aligned}]"] ["answer-77498169-1361-5d9a-8c47-6032457435c9" :answer/id #uuid "77498169-1361-5d9a-8c47-6032457435c9"] ["answer-77498169-1361-5d9a-8c47-6032457435c9" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-77498169-1361-5d9a-8c47-6032457435c9" :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}-y & -x \\\\ -x & 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["answer-7cfd7658-f969-5d24-b54b-e78400ec350a" :answer/id #uuid "7cfd7658-f969-5d24-b54b-e78400ec350a"] ["answer-7cfd7658-f969-5d24-b54b-e78400ec350a" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-7cfd7658-f969-5d24-b54b-e78400ec350a" :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}6x & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["answer-1845ba91-aa39-523c-b7fb-24b0540f22a4" :answer/id #uuid "1845ba91-aa39-523c-b7fb-24b0540f22a4"] ["answer-1845ba91-aa39-523c-b7fb-24b0540f22a4" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-1845ba91-aa39-523c-b7fb-24b0540f22a4" :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}6x & -x \\\\ -x & 0\\end{aligned}]"] [17592186155667 :answer-field/correct "answer-7cfd7658-f969-5d24-b54b-e78400ec350a"] [17592186155667 :answer-field/choices "answer-42ad8ac2-0cae-5d02-b554-16bcbaa98c5d"] [17592186155667 :answer-field/choices "answer-9734b10a-54a0-50b1-8bf9-29f1e1b884d0"] [17592186155667 :answer-field/choices "answer-77498169-1361-5d9a-8c47-6032457435c9"] [17592186155667 :answer-field/choices "answer-7cfd7658-f969-5d24-b54b-e78400ec350a"] [17592186155667 :answer-field/choices "answer-1845ba91-aa39-523c-b7fb-24b0540f22a4"] ["question-b2d69fc5-a88d-5940-a2a9-d7cc001b13e7" :question/id #uuid "b2d69fc5-a88d-5940-a2a9-d7cc001b13e7"] ["question-b2d69fc5-a88d-5940-a2a9-d7cc001b13e7" :question/math-academy-id "q-81033"] ["question-b2d69fc5-a88d-5940-a2a9-d7cc001b13e7" :question/problem "Find ${f}^{″}(1,\\pi )$ for the function $f(x,y)={x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y.$"] ["question-b2d69fc5-a88d-5940-a2a9-d7cc001b13e7" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R,$ given by\n\n$$\nf:{{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}⟶f({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nthe second derivative of $f$ is given by the $n\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}^{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the first derivative of $f(x,y),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x,y) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & \\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y) & \\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y & {x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the second partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y)=2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)=2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y)=-{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x,y) & =[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡y & 2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y \\\\ 2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y & -{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate this matrix at $(1,\\pi ).$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(1,\\pi )=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-b2d69fc5-a88d-5940-a2a9-d7cc001b13e7" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard] ["answer-field-dc17abaf-f11c-5b72-9671-ca1fd6cb7d81" :answer-field/id #uuid "dc17abaf-f11c-5b72-9671-ca1fd6cb7d81"] ["answer-ba9c170b-091c-52e8-887d-30f59a09cad0" :answer/id #uuid "ba9c170b-091c-52e8-887d-30f59a09cad0"] ["answer-ba9c170b-091c-52e8-887d-30f59a09cad0" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-ba9c170b-091c-52e8-887d-30f59a09cad0" :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]"] ["answer-62703d69-369b-5ace-a8d1-0c23e81a72c7" :answer/id #uuid "62703d69-369b-5ace-a8d1-0c23e81a72c7"] ["answer-62703d69-369b-5ace-a8d1-0c23e81a72c7" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-62703d69-369b-5ace-a8d1-0c23e81a72c7" :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}]"] ["answer-5c6f1e5c-0d83-5707-9be7-6186e6c7f868" :answer/id #uuid "5c6f1e5c-0d83-5707-9be7-6186e6c7f868"] ["answer-5c6f1e5c-0d83-5707-9be7-6186e6c7f868" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-5c6f1e5c-0d83-5707-9be7-6186e6c7f868" :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["answer-8a6bad3b-8668-59c6-b072-43c794a5f205" :answer/id #uuid "8a6bad3b-8668-59c6-b072-43c794a5f205"] ["answer-8a6bad3b-8668-59c6-b072-43c794a5f205" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-8a6bad3b-8668-59c6-b072-43c794a5f205" :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]"] ["answer-359a8021-5740-5c7d-85ad-b70c09368f55" :answer/id #uuid "359a8021-5740-5c7d-85ad-b70c09368f55"] ["answer-359a8021-5740-5c7d-85ad-b70c09368f55" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-359a8021-5740-5c7d-85ad-b70c09368f55" :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]"] ["answer-field-dc17abaf-f11c-5b72-9671-ca1fd6cb7d81" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-dc17abaf-f11c-5b72-9671-ca1fd6cb7d81" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-dc17abaf-f11c-5b72-9671-ca1fd6cb7d81" :answer-field/correct "answer-5c6f1e5c-0d83-5707-9be7-6186e6c7f868"] ["answer-field-dc17abaf-f11c-5b72-9671-ca1fd6cb7d81" :answer-field/choices "answer-ba9c170b-091c-52e8-887d-30f59a09cad0"] ["answer-field-dc17abaf-f11c-5b72-9671-ca1fd6cb7d81" :answer-field/choices "answer-62703d69-369b-5ace-a8d1-0c23e81a72c7"] ["answer-field-dc17abaf-f11c-5b72-9671-ca1fd6cb7d81" :answer-field/choices "answer-5c6f1e5c-0d83-5707-9be7-6186e6c7f868"] ["answer-field-dc17abaf-f11c-5b72-9671-ca1fd6cb7d81" :answer-field/choices "answer-8a6bad3b-8668-59c6-b072-43c794a5f205"] ["answer-field-dc17abaf-f11c-5b72-9671-ca1fd6cb7d81" :answer-field/choices "answer-359a8021-5740-5c7d-85ad-b70c09368f55"] ["question-b2d69fc5-a88d-5940-a2a9-d7cc001b13e7" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-dc17abaf-f11c-5b72-9671-ca1fd6cb7d81"] [17592186157425 :knowledge-point/questions "question-b2d69fc5-a88d-5940-a2a9-d7cc001b13e7"] ["question-46310383-5e9b-5711-9143-446211dee40a" :question/id #uuid "46310383-5e9b-5711-9143-446211dee40a"] ["question-46310383-5e9b-5711-9143-446211dee40a" :question/math-academy-id "q-80945"] ["question-46310383-5e9b-5711-9143-446211dee40a" :question/problem "Find ${f}^{″}(0,-\\frac{\\pi }{2})$ for the function $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x-y).$"] ["question-46310383-5e9b-5711-9143-446211dee40a" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R,$ given by\n\n$$\nf:{{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}⟶f({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nthe second derivative of $f$ is given by the $n\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}^{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the first derivative of $f(x,y),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x,y) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & \\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x-y)) & \\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x-y))\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x-y) & -\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x-y)\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the second partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x-y))=-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x-y)\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x-y))=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x-y) \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x-y))=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x-y)\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x-y))=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x-y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x,y) & =[\\begin{aligned}-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x-y) & 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x-y) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x-y) & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x-y)\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate this matrix at $(0,-\\frac{\\pi }{2}).$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(0,-\\frac{\\pi }{2})=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-46310383-5e9b-5711-9143-446211dee40a" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard] ["answer-field-a8dc6b69-1ae0-561f-a21b-1f490d47e054" :answer-field/id #uuid "a8dc6b69-1ae0-561f-a21b-1f490d47e054"] ["answer-9df6896f-980a-5433-b50d-177ed45dbdf5" :answer/id